  "findings": [
    "Identities, ages at arrival, payer, acuity and encounter history are internally consistent across all 108 month/facility strata and the carry-in, continuous-transfer, death and open-stay strata. Worker roles, assignment revisions, FTE and credentials are unchanged from version 1.0.2.",
    "Revised timing reads naturally in local time: inpatient home discharges fall in the late morning to evening after a ward-round readiness time; treat-and-release ED visits last roughly 1.5 to 8 hours; admitted ED visits carry a boarding tail; left-without-being-seen visits end within an hour.",
    "Quarterly notes cover COPD, pneumonia, diabetes, chest pain and abdominal pain contexts. Note times match encounter arrival and discharge; facts are grounded to recorded observations, problems and dispensed medication.",
    "Denials, appeals, write-offs, self-pay balances and draft-at-cutoff accounts appear across payers and settings in proportions consistent with the full-population checks.",
    "Capacity-driven external transfers rose from 539 to 625 because bed turnaround and placement now take realistic time; one patient died while awaiting placement and is handled as a boarding death. This is a moderate, explained change.",
    "Pre-existing (version 1.0) observation, unchanged: an inpatient transferred out after 24 hours awaiting a compatible bed receives a discharge summary whose final labs already show recovery. Recorded as P3 in the issue register; not a release blocker."
  ],
  "limitations_accepted": true,
  "limitations": [
    "Configured fictional adult pathways and template-driven notes are not population epidemiology, clinical effectiveness or treatment guidance.",
    "Thirty selected late-window terminal outcomes are boundary tests, not a mortality or survival population series. Mortality forecasting is outside this accepted scope.",
    "Selected services, stock and sparse support/admin attendance do not represent complete hospital billing, cost or payroll. Bundled demonstration charges are not a validated reimbursement tariff.",
    "Access grants are a selected revocation-history cohort, not every active authorized user.",
    "The fixed fictional catchment and public name distributions are shared across seeds; additional seeds test connected history sensitivity rather than independent demographic sampling.",
    "Joint-cell Wilson intervals are descriptive within month/facility/class. Repeat visits are correlated; sparse cells receive counts, intervals and domain constraints rather than arbitrary percentage gates or population-inference claims.",
    "Axiom covers twelve illustrative archetypes, with no customer layout/vendor certification and no claim of implementing approximately 900 customer reports. Workday/Axiom interfaces are local source simulations.",
    "Age 100 at the opening baseline may naturally age to 103. Unknown/censored outcomes, missing plans and zero plans remain separate.",
    "Version 1.1 ED stay, discharge timing, bed placement/cleaning, weekday mix, no-show, denial and RN absence behaviours are configured assumptions checked for internal plausibility, not benchmarks of a real hospital.",
    "RN overtime remains under 1% of RN hours because the fixed RN pool exceeds shift demand; overtime forecasting is outside the accepted scope.",
    "Phase 9 clean-environment release certification and explicit final data acceptance of version 1.1.0 are pending. No analytics solution, live integration, forecasting model, dashboard or agent is authorized by this review."
  ],
